# The Velvet Claw's people, in the hub (levels/hub/hub.gd, prologue.gd): Bastion at the door, the sisters in their
# rooms in the vaults, Vesper. Short lines in each voice (docs/WRITING.md); they change as the worlds are done.
# (Choices hang off the line before them: keep an unconditional line there, or a skipped [if] line takes them too.)

~ bastion
[if done/pier] Bastion: Good.
[if not done/pier] Bastion: Members.

# OWNER REVIEW: the sisters' scenes (WO-014b), opt-in, either way round, with any of them. A check-in first, aftercare
# after (hub/sessions.dialogue, core/cross_scene.gd), and "red" always ends it well. "The cross" is a scene on the
# vaults' cross (core/cross_scene.gd): "club/cross/<sister>_dom" Nim leads, "_sub" she does.

# Every sister is away on her own world's job until Nim finishes it (core/sisters.gd; owner, 2026-11-13). The first
# talk at home is her homecoming (<who>_home, which sets home/<who>); her first good scene at home earns her Rose.

~ augusta
[if not home/augusta] => augusta_home
Augusta: Posture, Nim. A Domme stands as though the room were hers. Because it is.
- Ask her for a scene. => augusta_scene
- Leave her be. => END

~ augusta_home
Augusta [warm]: Forty years of invitations, and the one year I go, we bring the house down. Worth the wait.
Augusta: Swyne's right hand is explaining himself to a committee. He keeps bowing. Nobody asked him to.
set home/augusta
Augusta: Now. You've been slouching while I was out. I can tell from here.
- Ask her for a scene. => augusta_scene
- Welcome home, Augusta. => END

~ augusta_scene
Augusta: Oh, how lovely. And which of us is in charge?
- You are. => augusta_switch
- I am. => augusta_domme
- The cross. => augusta_cross
- Another time. => END

~ augusta_switch
Augusta: Then stand for me. Feet together, chin level, tail balanced. I'll talk you through it.
Augusta: If it's too much, "red". "Yellow" and we rest a moment. I'll ask how you are, halfway.
Nim: Red. Yellow. Yes, Augusta.
set club/scene/augusta_switch
=> END

~ augusta_domme
Augusta: I'll hold a posture for you, and I'll get it wrong. Mostly on purpose. Correct me.
Augusta: My word is "red". And do remember to ask how I am. It's terribly attractive.
set club/scene/augusta_domme
=> END

~ augusta_cross
Augusta: The cross. Mm. And who's going on it, darling?
- You. I'll lead. => augusta_cross_dom
- Me. You lead. => augusta_cross_sub
- Another time. => END

~ augusta_cross_dom
Augusta: Then we'll do the form properly. My word is "red".
set club/cross/augusta_dom
=> END

~ augusta_cross_sub
Augusta: Then up you go, and we'll do the form properly. Your word is "red". Use it whenever you like.
set club/cross/augusta_sub
=> END

~ silke
[if not home/silke] => silke_home
[narrator] Silke looks up from a coil of rope, nods once, and goes back to it.
- Ask her for a scene. => silke_scene
- Leave her be. => END

~ silke_home
[narrator] Silke's back, salt still in her fur, coiling the same rope she took to the Docks. The harbour master's tie is still in it.
[narrator] She looks at the crane key on your belt, then at you.
set home/silke
Silke: Keep it.
- Ask her for a scene. => silke_scene
- Leave her be. => END

~ silke_scene
Silke: Mm. Which way round?
- You lead. => silke_switch
- I'll lead. => silke_domme
- The cross. => silke_cross
- Another time. => END

~ silke_switch
Silke: Arms, then. Over the sleeves. Nothing tight.
Silke: Your word is "red". "Yellow" and I loosen. I'll ask you, halfway.
Nim: Red. Yellow. Got it.
Silke: Breathe with me.
set club/scene/silke_switch
=> END

~ silke_domme
Silke: You? Tie me? ...All right.
Silke: My word's "red". Ask me how I'm doing, now and then. Properly.
Nim: I will.
set club/scene/silke_domme
=> END

~ silke_cross
Silke: The cross. Who's going on it?
- You. I'll lead. => silke_cross_dom
- Me. You lead. => silke_cross_sub
- Another time. => END

~ silke_cross_dom
Silke: Rope, then. My word's "red".
set club/cross/silke_dom
=> END

~ silke_cross_sub
Silke: Up you go. Your word's "red". I'll be listening for it.
set club/cross/silke_sub
=> END

~ rivet
# Talking to her also hands in seized contraband (levels/hub/hub.gd _hand_in): lures and upgrades. While she's at
# the Press, her drop box takes it (rivet_box).
[if not home/rivet] => rivet_home
Rivet: The muzzle's holding up? Good. I built it to outlast your bad decisions.
Rivet: Bring me every one of Swyne's toys you seize. Gutted, they make good distractions.
- That's all. => END
- A scene? => rivet_scene
- The cross? => rivet_cross

~ rivet_home
Rivet [grin]: Back. The Press is running in reverse and printing apologies. I'm told Swyne read one. Out loud. Twice.
Rivet: My courier says you've been stuffing my box the whole time. Good girl. Here, a welcome-home present.
set home/rivet
Rivet: From now on, hand the toys to me. It's faster, and I like to watch them come apart.
- Thanks, Rivet. => END
- A scene? => rivet_scene

~ rivet_box
[narrator] A sturdy crate by Rivet's dark bench, a slot in the lid. A card taped to it: "TOYS IN. GEAR OUT. COURIER NIGHTLY. DON'T TOUCH THE BENCH. R."
=> END

~ rivet_scene
Rivet: I've made cuffs. Somebody has to wear them, and somebody has to fasten them. Which are you?
- Fit them on me. => rivet_switch
- I'll fasten yours. => rivet_domme
- Never mind. => END

~ rivet_switch
Rivet: Arms out. Tell me when each one's snug. Not tight. Snug. There's a difference and I'll be grading it.
Rivet: Your word's "red". I'll ask your colour halfway, because I ask everyone everything.
set club/scene/rivet_switch
=> END

~ rivet_domme
Rivet: Fasten them, then check every buckle. Every one. I made them, so I'll know.
Rivet: My word's "red".
set club/scene/rivet_domme
=> END

~ rivet_cross
Rivet: The cross. Which of us is on it?
- You. I'll lead. => rivet_cross_dom
- Me. You lead. => rivet_cross_sub
- Never mind. => END

~ rivet_cross_dom
Rivet: Cuffs. I'll inspect the buckles from the inside. My word's "red".
set club/cross/rivet_dom
=> END

~ rivet_cross_sub
Rivet: Your muzzle stays on; it's mine and it's good. Your word's "red".
set club/cross/rivet_sub
=> END

~ dash
[if not home/dash] => dash_home
Dash [grin]: Nobody books me. Can't think why.
Dash: I hit the bag. The bag doesn't complain. It's the healthiest relationship in the building.
- A scene? => dash_scene
- The cross? => dash_cross
- Keep hitting it. => END

~ dash_home
Dash [grin]: Home! Look at my bag. It missed me. It's swinging with joy. Or because I hit it.
[if pier/race_won] Dash: You took Laffer apart and beat me in a race. I'm telling everyone I let you.
[if not pier/race_won] Dash: You took Laffer apart. I won a race. We both had a big night.
set home/dash
Dash: Book me sometime. Nobody ever does. It's a whole thing.
- A scene? => dash_scene
- Welcome home, Dash. => END

~ dash_scene
Dash [grin]: Someone booked me! Okay. Okay okay. Who's in charge?
- You are. => dash_switch
- I am. => dash_domme
- Never mind. => END

~ dash_switch
Dash: Drill! I call it, you hit it. High, low, left, right. It gets faster. It always gets faster.
Dash: Your word's "red". I'll ask halfway. I'll remember to ask halfway. Probably.
set club/scene/dash_switch
=> END

~ dash_domme
Dash: Hold me still. Bet you can't. I'm going to wriggle, and that's not a colour, that's just me.
Dash: My word's "red". If I say it, I mean it, even if I'm laughing.
set club/scene/dash_domme
=> END

~ dash_cross
Dash [grin]: Ooh. Who's on it?
- You. I'll lead. => dash_cross_dom
- Me. You lead. => dash_cross_sub
- Never mind. => END

~ dash_cross_dom
Dash: I'm going to wriggle. That's not a colour, that's just me. My word's "red". Probably won't need it. Might.
set club/cross/dash_dom
=> END

~ dash_cross_sub
Dash: Ha! Okay. Your word's "red". I'll be gentle. Mostly. I'll ask!
set club/cross/dash_sub
=> END

~ lull
[if not home/lull] => lull_home
Lull: Mm. Swyne took something gentle and made a weapon of it. We took it back.
- A scene? => lull_scene
- The cross? => lull_cross
- Rest well. => END

~ lull_home
Lull [warm]: Home. The Retreat's guests are waking up one by one, and every one of them is furious with the doctor. It's lovely to hear.
set home/lull
Lull: A week of pretending to be one of them. I need tea, cushions, and something gentle. Sit with me sometime.
- A scene? => lull_scene
- Rest well. => END

~ lull_scene
Lull: Something quiet. Which of us wears the blindfold?
- You lead. I'll wear it. => lull_switch
- I'll lead. You wear it. => lull_domme
- Not tonight. => END

~ lull_switch
Lull: I'll count, slowly. Breathe on each one. Nothing else to do. Nothing else to be.
Lull: Your word is "red". I'll ask your colour halfway, softly.
set club/scene/lull_switch
=> END

~ lull_domme
Lull: I like not knowing where you'll be. Don't rush. The waiting is the best part.
Lull: My word is "red". And ask me how I am. I'll tell you the truth.
set club/scene/lull_domme
=> END

~ lull_cross
Lull: The cross. Mm. Which of us?
- You. I'll lead. => lull_cross_dom
- Me. You lead. => lull_cross_sub
- Not tonight. => END

~ lull_cross_dom
Lull: Slowly, please. My word is "red". I'll say it if I need to; I always do.
set club/cross/lull_dom
=> END

~ lull_cross_sub
Lull: Come. Your word is "red". I'll be very quiet, and very close.
set club/cross/lull_sub
=> END

~ grizelda
[if not home/grizelda] => grizelda_home
Grizelda: Shoes. Wipe.
- A scene? => grizelda_scene
- The cross? => grizelda_cross
- Yes, Grizelda. => END

~ grizelda_home
Grizelda: The Close is quiet. Net curtains still. Marjorie Gander sitting down for once in her life.
Grizelda: Twelve years I waited to see that. You took one evening. Hmph.
set home/grizelda
Grizelda: Shoes. Wipe. And if you want a scene, ask properly.
- A scene? => grizelda_scene
- Yes, Grizelda. => END

~ grizelda_scene
Grizelda: Hm. And who sits on the throne?
- You do. => grizelda_switch
- I do. => grizelda_domme
- Never mind. => END

~ grizelda_switch
Grizelda: Then you kneel, and my boots get polished. Small circles. Not too fast. I will inspect.
Grizelda: Your word is "red". I'll ask your colour halfway, and I'll want a real answer.
set club/scene/grizelda_switch
=> END

~ grizelda_domme
Grizelda: You, on my throne. ...Fine. Make me do as I'm told. I won't make it easy.
Grizelda: My word is "red". I won't need it. Ask me how I am anyway.
set club/scene/grizelda_domme
=> END

~ grizelda_cross
Grizelda: Hm. And who's on it?
- You. I'll lead. => grizelda_cross_dom
- Me. You lead. => grizelda_cross_sub
- Never mind. => END

~ grizelda_cross_dom
Grizelda: You'll lead and I'll tell you how. My word is "red". I won't need it.
set club/cross/grizelda_dom
=> END

~ grizelda_cross_sub
Grizelda: Up. Your word is "red", and I'll respect it faster than you can say it.
set club/cross/grizelda_sub
=> END

~ vesper
# OWNER REVIEW
[if not done/pier] Vesper [calm]: The Pier, Nim. East across the square, down Seafront Road. Dash is waiting.
[if not done/pier] Vesper: Find me on the wheel if you need me. I'll be watching.
[if done/pier] Vesper [warm]: Primrose Close next. Grizelda will meet you there.
[if done/pier] Vesper: The Close won't open its gate to a beginner. A few more roses first.
[if done/pier] Vesper: And welcome Dash home properly. She's been telling the punch bag about the Pier for an hour.
